{{!
    @template core/login_layout

    Modern UI override of the login-flow layout (login, MFA...).

    Split (default): brand panel on the left from the lg breakpoint, form on the right. Below lg the panel is
    hidden and a short welcome is shown above the form instead.
    Centered (mu_centered): no side panel; the form card sits centred over the brand background, with the welcome
    above it at every width.

    Context variables (from theme_modernui's layout/login.php; all optional, so other login-flow pages that render
    this partial without them still get the split layout with core's default copy):
    * output - The core renderer (main_content).
    * mu_centered - True for the centred layout.
    * mu_welcometitle - Welcome heading (plain text, already formatted).
    * mu_welcometext - Welcome text (HTML, already formatted).
    * mu_compactlogo - Compact logo URL, if the site has one.
    * sitename - Site short name.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "output": {"main_content": "<h1>Login form goes here</h1>"},
        "mu_centered": false,
        "mu_welcometitle": "Welcome to Example Academy",
        "mu_welcometext": "<p>Learn at your own pace.</p>",
        "mu_compactlogo": null,
        "sitename": "Example"
    }
}}
<div id="page-content" class="mu-login min-vh-100 row g-0">
    {{^mu_centered}}
    <aside class="login-layout-left col-lg-6 d-none d-lg-flex">
        {{> core/login_panel }}
    </aside>
    {{/mu_centered}}
    <div id="region-main" class="login-layout-right col-12{{^mu_centered}} col-lg-6{{/mu_centered}}">
        <div id="region-main-box" class="login-layout-right-content">
            {{#mu_welcometext}}
            <div class="mu-login-intro{{^mu_centered}} d-lg-none{{/mu_centered}}">
                {{#mu_welcometitle}}<p class="mu-login-intro-title">{{mu_welcometitle}}</p>{{/mu_welcometitle}}
                <div class="mu-login-intro-text">{{{mu_welcometext}}}</div>
            </div>
            {{/mu_welcometext}}
            <div class="login-container">
                {{{ output.main_content }}}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
